113
00:08:21.767 --> 00:08:22.918
(narrator) Verse 3, the iceberg.

114
00:08:22.918 --> 00:08:26.918
(narrator) A leader connects the exposed tip to Interface: what callers can rely on.

115
00:08:26.918 --> 00:08:29.494
(narrator) A checkmarked note says Same promised behavior.

116
00:08:29.494 --> 00:08:34.536
(narrator) Below the waterline, turning gears give way to a yellow submarine while the tip stays fixed.

117
00:08:34.536 --> 00:08:40.345
(narrator) Three choice switches change below the water: array or hash table, cache or no cache, MongoDB or Supabase.

118
00:08:40.345 --> 00:08:42.647
(narrator) New internals must keep the same contract.

119
00:08:42.647 --> 00:08:48.237
(narrator) Then a connected cutaway shows an electricity source, the grid, a wall outlet, a charger, and a phone.

120
00:08:48.237 --> 00:08:51.361
(narrator) Solar panels at noon change to wind turbines at midnight.

121
00:08:51.361 --> 00:08:57.061
(narrator) The grid continues supplying the same voltage and frequency at the outlet, and the phone keeps charging.

122
00:08:57.061 --> 00:09:00.788
(narrator) The outlet is the interface; the plant is the hidden implementation.

123
00:09:01.393 --> 00:09:04.293
♪ Picture an iceberg. The tip’s the interface: ♪

124
00:09:04.293 --> 00:09:07.153
