161
00:11:32.492 --> 00:11:39.511
(narrator) Four questions try the idea on new cases: a sort algorithm, prices in cents, a payment method's return type, and a database swap.

162
00:11:40.127 --> 00:11:43.727
♪ Pop quiz! Y2K: what got copied everywhere? ♪

163
00:11:43.727 --> 00:11:45.167
♪ (crowd) The two-digit year! ♪

164
00:11:45.167 --> 00:11:48.267
♪ Your sort is quicksort. Secret, or contract? ♪

165
00:11:48.267 --> 00:11:50.847
♪ (crowd) Secret! They just want it sorted! ♪

166
00:11:50.847 --> 00:11:53.847
